{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZCV1zH1ovoDqGAizEd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ADT acquisition gives a view of how Thrive Holdings says it works with OpenAI. According to the article, OpenAI supplies the companies in Thrive's portfolio with AI models and technology, and also with people: forward-deployed engineers, who are OpenAI staff placed inside the businesses. Thrive Holdings, a holding company spun out of Thrive Capital, says it holds over 75 companies and aims to keep them long-term while revitalizing them with AI. OpenAI is both an investor in it and a partner.\n\nADT is the largest deal the article describes. Thrive is paying $10 per share, about $7.6 billion in equity, and ADT puts the total enterprise value at $15.3 billion. The companies have not said what AI-powered security products will come out of it. They said only that they plan to invest and release new ones, and that ADT will be the foundation of Thrive Holdings' smart home security business.\n\nThat leaves the central claim untested for now. The AI-revitalization model is Thrive's own description of its strategy, and the article reports no results from it, either at ADT or at the other portfolio companies. What can be observed is the market around it. Apple has entered home security with LG and Schneider Electric, Amazon has updated its smart home line with AI-powered cameras, and ADT already partners with Apple and Google and is expected to continue doing so. Whatever Thrive and ADT build will arrive alongside products from companies that are also ADT's partners."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":2026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":812},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_t